<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Appreciation: value of land after T years (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A plot of land near {@town@} is bought for Ksh \( {@P0@} \). Its value appreciates at a steady rate of \( {@R0@}\% \) per annum.</p>
<p>Give your answers to the nearest shilling.</p>
<p>(a) Find the value of the land after \( {@T0@} \) years.</p>
<div>Value \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) By how much has the value of the land increased over the \( {@T0@} \) years?</p>
<div>Increase \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> Appreciation works like compound interest: each year's increase is calculated on the value at the start of that year.</p>
\[ A = P\left(1 + \frac{R}{100}\right)^T = {@P0@}\left(1 + \frac{ {@R0@} }{100}\right)^{ {@T0@} } = {@P0@} \times ({@float(1 + R0/100)@})^{ {@T0@} } = {@round(A0)@}. \]
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Increase \( = A - P = {@round(A0)@} - {@P0@} = {@round(A0) - P0@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
